# Shortcuts Widget — 5 Layout Variants

Grounded in the current model: `items[]` (each `kind: instance|dashboard|url`, `ref`, optional `label`, `icon`), a `variant`, and `newTab`. Today only `list` + `grid` exist. Below are 5 distinct layout directions.

Icon legend (lucide): ▣ instance (Box) · ▦ dashboard (LayoutDashboard) · ◍ url (Globe)

---

## 1. Compact List  (refines today's `list`)

Dense single-column rows. Icon + label, kind-tinted icon, chevron + faint target on hover. Best when shortcuts are mixed and many.

```
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│ Shortcuts                     │  ← widget.title
├──────────────────────────────┤
│ ▦  Q3 Pipeline            ›   │
│ ▣  Acme Corp                  │
│ ▣  Renewal — Globex           │
│ ◍  Stripe Dashboard       ↗   │  ← ↗ = newTab url
│ ▦  Team Overview              │
└──────────────────────────────┘
   hover row → bg-accent, › chevron fades in
```

- Uses: `label` (or resolved name), `icon`/kind icon, `newTab` → ↗ glyph on urls.
- Cheap win: add a right-aligned chevron `›` (internal) / `↗` (new-tab url) so target type reads at a glance.

---

## 2. Icon Tiles  (refines today's `grid`)

Responsive auto-fit cards, icon chip on top, label below, kind accent bar. Reads like a launchpad. Best for ≤8 hero links.

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Shortcuts                             │
├──────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐     │
│ │   ▦    │ │   ▣    │ │   ◍    │     │
│ │ Q3 Pipe│ │  Acme  │ │ Stripe │     │
│ └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘     │
│ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐     │
│ │   ▣    │ │   ▦    │ │   ◍    │     │
│ │ Globex │ │ Team   │ │ Docs ↗ │     │
│ └────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘     │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘
   auto-fit: cols flex with tile width (1→4), not fixed 2
```

- Uses: `icon`/kind icon (18px), `label`, kind color accent on chip.
- Upgrade vs today: `grid-cols-2` → `auto-fill minmax()` so it adapts to the flexbox tile size.

---

## 3. Launchpad Buttons

Full-width prominent rows. Icon in a rounded chip, bold label, optional subtitle = resolved target. Best when there are a few important jump-offs and the tile is wide.

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Quick links                             │
├────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ┌────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│ │ ▦   Q3 Pipeline                  › │ │
│ │     dashboard                      │ │
│ └────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│ ┌────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│ │ ◍   Stripe                       ↗ │ │
│ │     dashboard.stripe.com           │ │
│ └────────────────────────────────────┘ │
│ ┌────────────────────────────────────┐ │
│ │ ▣   Acme Corp                    › │ │
│ │     Account                        │ │
│ └────────────────────────────────────┘ │
└────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- Uses: chip(`icon`), `label`, subtitle = host (url) / concept name (instance) / "Dashboard".
- New behavior: subtitle line, derived — no new config field required.

---

## 4. Grouped Sections

Auto-groups items by `kind` under subtle headers. Scales cleanly to many shortcuts; reads like a mini nav. Best for 10+ mixed items.

```
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│ Shortcuts                     │
├──────────────────────────────┤
│ DASHBOARDS                    │
│   ▦  Q3 Pipeline              │
│   ▦  Team Overview            │
│                               │
│ RECORDS                       │
│   ▣  Acme Corp                │
│   ▣  Renewal — Globex         │
│                               │
│ LINKS                         │
│   ◍  Stripe          ↗        │
│   ◍  Notion HQ       ↗        │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

- Uses: groups by `kind`; headers only shown for non-empty groups (mirrors ConceptSelect Org/Integration grouping pattern).
- Optional config: `grouped: boolean` to toggle vs flat list. Order preserved within group.

---

## 5. Chip Flow

Wrapping flow of compact rounded chips (icon + label). Fills width, wraps to height — ideal for narrow OR wide tiles where a column wastes space. Best for short labels.

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Shortcuts                             │
├──────────────────────────────────────┤
│  (▦ Q3 Pipeline) (▣ Acme) (◍ Stripe↗)│
│  (▣ Globex) (▦ Team) (◍ Docs↗)        │
│  (▣ Renewal) (◍ Notion↗)              │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘
   flex-wrap; chip = pill, bg-muted, hover bg-accent
```

- Uses: `icon`/kind icon (14px), `label`, `↗` suffix for new-tab urls.
- Density king: most links per square inch; degrades gracefully at any tile size.

---

## Comparison

| Variant      | Density | Best for                | New config?            |
|--------------|---------|-------------------------|------------------------|
| Compact List | High    | many mixed items        | none (chevron polish)  |
| Icon Tiles   | Medium  | ≤8 hero links           | none (auto-fit cols)   |
| Launchpad    | Low     | few important, wide tile| none (derived subtitle)|
| Grouped      | Medium  | 10+ items, nav feel     | `grouped?: boolean`    |
| Chip Flow    | V.High  | short labels, any shape | `variant: "chips"`     |

All five reuse the existing `ShortcutItem` model and `newTab`. Only Grouped + Chip Flow imply an additive optional contract field; the rest are pure render changes.
